<title>USA: Jabil Circuit Q3 shr $0.76 vs $0.33.</title>
<headline>Jabil Circuit Q3 shr $0.76 vs $0.33.</headline>
<dateline>ST. PETERSBURG, Fla. 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In thousands, except for per share data)</p>
<p>				Three months ended  Nine months ended</p>
<p>				   May 31,  May 31,  May 31,  May 31,</p>
<p>					1996     1997     1996     1997</p>
<p> Net revenue		  $219,701 $247,637 $689,184 $672,894</p>
<p>   Cost of revenue	   201,142  215,603  635,039  591,292</p>
<p> Gross profit		   18,559   32,034   54,145   81,602</p>
<p>Operating expenses:</p>
<p>Selling, general and</p>
<p>     administrative	    6,612    9,252   18,243   24,897</p>
<p>   Research and development    576	723    1,503    2,232</p>
<p> Operating income	     11,371   22,059   34,399   54,473</p>
<p>   Interest expense	    1,768	406    6,754    1,453</p>
<p> Income before income taxes  9,603   21,653   27,645   53,020</p>
<p>   Income taxes		  3,366    7,081    9,855   18,561</p>
<p> Net income			6,237   14,572   17,790   34,459</p>
<p> Net income per share	   0.33     0.76     0.98     1.80</p>
<p>Weighted average number of</p>
<p>shares of common stock and</p>
<p>common stock equivalents</p>
<p>				    18,893   19,196   18,226   19,100</p>
<p>NOTE: Company announced a two-for-one stock split, to be effected through the issuance of a 100 percent stock dividend. The record date is July 8 and shares will be distributed on July 22. The dividend will raise the number of common shares outstanding to 36.6 million, from 18.3 million.</p>
<p>Full company name is Jabil Circuit Inc.</p>
